# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: dcl-ncurses-renderer — a full-screen ncurses DCL renderer, parallel to the line TUI
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: feature
#+DEPENDS: dcl-tui-completion (TUI renderer DONE), grread (input model)
#+BRANCH: feature-dcl-ncurses

* Context / motivation (pjb, 2026-09-12)

DCL should have THREE parallel UIs: the line-oriented terminal renderer (the
"dumb" style), a full-screen ncurses renderer, and the Qt GUI (subprocess,
opendcl epic). Today only ONE terminal renderer exists — =autolisp-dcl/source/
terminal.lisp=, a line-oriented (cooked) renderer that paints the tile tree once
then reads =key= / =key=value= / =key==value= / =key!= commands via =read-line=.
It is UI-agnostic (runs the same under the dumb or ncurses DEBUGGER UI, or none):
the dumb/ncurses distinction exists only for the debugger, not for DCL. There is
NO ncurses-native DCL rendering. This issue builds it, so the line (dumb) and
full-screen (ncurses) DCL paths are genuinely parallel, and documents how widget
input is done in each.

* Design decisions (CONFIRMED by pjb, 2026-09-13)

- Navigation/activation: =:up/:down= + =Tab/Shift-Tab= move focus; =:enter= or
  =Space= activates/toggles the focused tile; printable chars edit a focused
  edit_box (=:backspace= deletes); =:left/:right= adjust a focused slider and
  move list/popup selection; =:escape= = cancel.
- Layout: 2-D honouring the DCL =:row= / =:column= geometry from the start (a
  real dialog look), NOT the one-tile-per-line fallback.
- Renderer selection: =--dcl auto= PREFERS ncurses when stdout is a TTY +
  curses available + no GUI configured; non-TTY stays the line TUI (the
  =-command= scenario); explicit =--dcl ncurses|tui= always honoured.

* Design

** Behaviour parity is the invariant
The ncurses renderer differs ONLY in presentation + input; the state machine is
shared. It reuses the runtime's action/reason plumbing and the terminal
renderer's value-tile helpers so tile values and =$reason= codes are byte-for-
byte identical to the line renderer:
- =dcl-runtime-fire-action (dialog key value reason)= (runtime.lisp:389),
  =dcl-reason-code= (runtime.lisp:378): selected=1 / changed=2 / lost-focus=3 /
  double-click=4.
- =terminal-handle-value-tile= (terminal.lisp:229), =terminal-select-radio=
  (:209), =terminal-handle-button= (:149), =terminal-fire-registered= (:323).
- =done_dialog= loop: run until =(dcl-dialog-finished-p dialog)=, return
  =(dcl-dialog-status dialog)= (1 OK / 0 Cancel).

** Draws against tui-core only (no bad deps)
The renderer targets the dependency-free =tui-core= screen protocol
(=clautolisp.ui.tui=): =tui-put (screen row col string &key attr)= (the only
string primitive; 0-based; =:attr= a face symbol), =tui-clear=, =tui-refresh=,
=tui-size= (=> rows cols=), =tui-read-key= (char or keyword), =tui-move-cursor=;
plus helpers =draw-box= / =pad-string= / =truncate-string=. It NEVER constructs
a curses screen — it accepts a screen object (real =curses-screen= or a
=mock-screen=). So =autolisp-dcl= gains a =tui-core= dependency (cycle-free;
tui-core depends on nothing); the libncurses backend stays on-demand at the CLI
(as the debugger already does via =ncurses-terminal-screen=, main.lisp:1229).

** Modal loop (mirrors ncurses-ui.lisp:668 ui-await-command)
=tui-start= → =unwind-protect= { redraw-all → =tui-read-key= → dispatch →
return when done } → =tui-stop=. Redraw = =tui-clear= + =tui-size= + walk the
tile tree drawing each tile, the focused one highlighted, + =tui-refresh=.

** Focus + navigation (DECISIONS — confirm)
- Focus ring = interactive tiles in source order, reusing
  =terminal-collect-interactive-keys= (terminal.lisp:126): button, edit_box,
  toggle, radio_button, list_box, popup_list, slider, image_button.
- Keys: =:up=/=:down= and =Tab=/=Shift-Tab= move focus; =:enter=/=Space=
  activate/toggle the focused tile; printable chars edit a focused edit_box
  (=:backspace= deletes); =:left=/=:right= adjust a focused slider and move the
  selection in a list/popup; =:escape= = cancel (is_cancel path). Enter on
  accept → done_dialog(1); on cancel → done_dialog(0).
- Focused tile drawn with a distinguishing face (new =:dcl-focus= face, or reuse
  =:selection=).

** Layout (DECISION — confirm)
Start SIMPLE: one interactive tile per line, vertical stack, containers add a
label + indentation (parallels the line renderer's presentation, full-screen
with highlight + in-place editing). A richer 2-D layout honouring =:row= /
=:column= geometry is a later enhancement, not this issue.

** Selection / install (main.lisp select-and-install-dcl-renderer:1972)
Add a =:ncurses= value to =--dcl tui|gui|ncurses|auto= (+ parser + help text).
=:ncurses= → source a screen from =ncurses-terminal-screen= (main.lisp:1229);
if curses is unavailable, warn + fall back to =make-terminal-renderer=. =:auto=
policy: keep non-TTY → line TUI (the =-command= scenario); when TTY +
=curses-available-p= + no GUI configured, =:auto= MAY prefer =:ncurses=
(DECISION — confirm whether auto should prefer ncurses over the line TUI when
interactive). =make-ncurses-renderer= must NOT self-install at load (unlike
terminal.lisp:410) — installation stays opt-in via the CLI.

* Progress

- Slice 1 DONE (clautolisp 2.2.16 / alfe 2.2.24): =ncurses-renderer.lisp= —
  =make-ncurses-renderer= (dcl-renderer shape, not self-installing) +
  =ncurses-run-dialog= modal loop over a tui-core screen; a 2-D :row/:column
  =%ncurses-layout=; text/button rendering (=[ label ]=); focus ring (reusing
  =terminal-collect-interactive-keys=) with =:up/:down/:tab= nav and the
  focused tile drawn =:selection=; Enter/Space activation (buttons via
  =terminal-handle-button=, other tiles via =terminal-handle-value-tile= for
  parity); Esc / key-stream EOF cancel (status 0). autolisp-dcl gains a
  cycle-free =tui-core= dep. 4 headless mock-screen tests in autolisp-dcl/tests;
  full =make -C clautolisp test-sbcl= green.

* Slices (each: full `make -C clautolisp test-sbcl` green, own MR, version bump)

1. Renderer skeleton + modal loop: =make-ncurses-renderer= (dcl-renderer struct,
   runtime.lisp:74) + =ncurses-run-dialog=; draw text/label/button tiles + focus
   ring; =:up/:down/:tab= navigation; Enter on accept/cancel → done_dialog;
   Escape → cancel. Headless tests (mock-screen: assert rendered lines, focus
   face via =mock-attr-at=, accept→1 / cancel→0).
2. Interactive value tiles: toggle (Space flips [x]/[ ]), radio_button/column
   (mutual exclusion), edit_box (type/backspace, reason=changed), slider
   (Left/Right clamp). Reuse terminal value-tile helpers; assert value
   round-trip via get_tile + rendered cell.
3. Lists + images: list_box / popup_list (in-place selection, Enter selects),
   image / image_button (activatable placeholder); wire set-tile / focus / mode
   / populate-list / image-paint fns to trigger a redraw.
4. CLI + docs: =--dcl ncurses= selection + auto gating (main.lisp), ASDF (new
   =autolisp-dcl/source/ncurses-renderer.lisp= + =tui-core= dep), and the
   DOCUMENTATION deliverable — extend the user manual "DCL dialogs" section with
   a per-widget input reference for BOTH the line (dumb) TUI (what you type:
   =key= / =key=value= / modifiers) AND the ncurses TUI (focus + activate/edit
   keys), per widget, and how =$reason= is produced in each.

* Acceptance

- Under =--dcl ncurses=, greet + all-widgets run headlessly through the ncurses
  renderer (mock-screen), every widget interactive, values round-trip through
  get_tile, all four =$reason= codes reachable — identical results to the line
  renderer.
- =--dcl ncurses= selection documented; auto/non-TTY fallback to line TUI kept.
- FiveAM tests (autolisp-dcl + builtins-core) cover each widget over the ncurses
  renderer via the mock screen; whole suite green in the FULL image
  (=make -C clautolisp test-sbcl=).
- User-manual "DCL dialogs" gains the per-widget input reference for the line
  and ncurses TUIs.

* Notes / references (from the 2026-09-12 API map)
- Screen protocol: =autolisp-debug-ui-tui/source/tui.lisp:9-26= (tui-put etc.),
  faces =faces.lisp=; curses backend =autolisp-debug-ui-tui-curses/source/
  curses.lisp= (every op real, libncurses on demand).
- Mock screen captures a char grid + face grid: =tui.lisp:104=; helpers
  =mock-grid-lines= / =mock-find-line= / =mock-attr-at= / =make-mock-screen
  :keys= / =mock-feed-keys=; scripted driver =run-ncurses= (ncurses tests
  package.lisp:47).
- Renderer contract: =dcl-renderer= struct runtime.lisp:74; copy the shape of
  =make-terminal-renderer= terminal.lisp:379 (do NOT copy its load-time
  install). Tile model: =dcl-tile= model.lisp; =tile-attribute= model.lisp:31.
- The Qt renderer (subprocess) is the third UI; its C++ side is the opendcl
  epic and out of scope here.
